4505: \begin{proposition}[Current-package acceptance and certificate ledger]
4506: \label{prop:current-package-acceptance-certificate-ledger}
4507: Let $P^{+}$ be the finite current package consisting of the primary source
4508: \path{submission_abstract.tex}, this supplement \path{main.tex}, and, under the
4509: exact-or-archive-equivalent support-surface condition of
4510: Proposition~\ref{audit:review-bundle-availability-condition},
4511: \path{review_bundle/REVIEW_BUNDLE_MANIFEST.json}, together with
4512: \path{review_bundle/certificate_schema.json},
4513: \path{review_bundle/current_package_pass_records.json},
4514: \path{review_bundle/submission_interface_map.json},
4515: \path{review_bundle/primary_claim_inventory.json},
4516: \path{review_bundle/verify_certificate_records.py},
4517: \path{review_bundle/certificate_verification_run.log}, and the explicit
4518: historical paths named in the case catalogue.  Root-level diagnostics such as
4519: \path{PIPELINE.md}, \path{SOURCE_MAP.md}, \path{ARTIFACT_INVENTORY.md}, and
4520: \path{source_interface_record.json} may explain local provenance or path-verified
4521: history, but they are not finite package coordinates for this proposition unless
4522: their contents are represented in \path{main.tex} or in the submitted support
4523: surface.  The TeX source fixes the displayed six-row ledger.  This state is denoted
4524: $P^{+}_{6}$ in Theorem~\ref{thm:nested-package-states}: it is the row-frozen
4525: certificate state for $a_1,\ldots,a_6$, before the submitted theorem-ledger
4526: coordinate $a_7$ is adjoined.  The review-bundle files in this definition are
4527: supplemental-record components: claims that depend on them are conditional on
4528: those files being submitted with matching paths and records, or on an archival
4529: equivalent satisfying Proposition~\ref{audit:review-bundle-availability-condition}.
4530: Tables~\ref{tab:current-acceptance-ledger}
4531: and~\ref{tab:current-certificate-ledger} form a finite submission-local
4532: acceptance-entry ledger for the load-bearing current-package claims used in
4533: Corollary~\ref{cor:current-package-path-verified-instantiation}.  For each entry
4534: $a_i$, the two tables determine the certificate fields
4535: \[
4536: \mathcal C(a_i)=(K_i,\ell_i,E_i,H_i,R_i,D_i,B_i)
4537: \]
4538: and each such certificate is locally checkable at the path-verified evidence
4539: level.  No load-bearing claim outside these six manually selected entries is
4540: accepted by the current-package instantiation.  This is completeness of the
4541: declared six-row package ledger only; it is not a deterministic extraction or
4542: completeness assertion for all theorem-like environments or all possible claims
4543: in \path{main.tex}.
4544: \end{proposition}
4545: 
4546: \begin{proof}
4547: The acceptance-entry ledger is finite because Table~\ref{tab:current-acceptance-ledger}
4548: has six rows.  Its rows enumerate exactly the assertions on which the current
4549: package corollary depends: the bounded imported source interface, the existence
4550: of the presentation-only package, and the four case-study lessons for intake
4551: isolation, overlap blocking, fake-extension rejection, and artifact limitation.
4552: The third column assigns the claim-kind set $K_i$ for each accepted assertion.
4553: These kinds all lie in the seven-kind domain of the dispatch function $\Gamma$.
4554: 
4555: For each row, Table~\ref{tab:current-certificate-ledger} supplies the remaining
4556: certificate fields.  The declared evidence level $\ell_i$ is path-verified in
4557: every row.  The durable manuscript contribution is the finite row text printed in
4558: the tables and the proof that these fields have the required schema shape.  The
4559: matching assertions about JSON mirrors, pass-record files, manifest entries, and
4560: verifier logs are supplemental-record assertions and require the named
4561: \path{review_bundle/} files to be present.  The evidence surface $E_i$ is a finite
4562: list of submission-local files, review-bundle records, pinned source-interface
4563: records, or explicit historical paths.  The promotion field $H_i$ is either the current active-paper marker
4564: \path{main.tex} together with \path{PIPELINE.md}, or the explicit marker that the
4565: case row does not itself cross a new route boundary.  The pass-record field
4566: $R_i$ names the finite gate records used by the row: source-interface extraction
4567: and consistency for $a_1$, package and submission-pack records for $a_2$,
4568: promotion for $a_3$, overlap and submission-state for $a_4$, theorem-content and
4569: discovery gating for $a_5$, and artifact status plus limitation-ledger gating for
4570: $a_6$.
4571: 
4572: The discovery field behaves exactly as required by the certificate schema.  It is
4573: present only for $a_5$, the row whose accepted claim has discovery kind, and it
4574: names the pinned source-interface rows that supply the certificate-and-ledger,
4575: demotion, lineage, pipeline-safety, and main-pipeline witnesses.  For the other
4576: rows the claim-kind set does not contain discovery, so $D_i$ is absent.  Finally,
4577: the boundary field $B_i$ records the same limitation in every row: the package is
4578: using path-verified evidence, not command-run evidence, unless the command,
4579: source commit, environment, exit code, and log path are explicitly recorded.
4580: Consequently the ledger is historical and path-verified; it does not assert a
4581: fresh Lean build, daemon pass, full-source rerun, Rule110 or GroundCompiler
4582: rerun, artifact-suite validation, or external venue acceptance.  Thus each row
4583: determines a locally checkable publication certificate
4584: \(\mathcal C(a_i)\).
4585: 
4586: It remains only to see that the ledger is complete for the declared
4587: current-package instantiation.  Corollary~\ref{cor:current-package-path-verified-instantiation}
4588: uses no unlisted positive claim: its source-interface premise is $a_1$, its
4589: package premise is $a_2$, and its four bounded case-study premises are
4590: $a_3$--$a_6$.  The proof does not claim that these six rows were produced by a
4591: complete theorem-environment extractor or that they enumerate every theorem-like
4592: obligation in this source; that stronger reading is isolated in
4593: Theorem~\ref{thm:manual-ledger-dependence-boundary}.  Any proposed stronger
4594: reading, such as a fresh full-source rebuild,
4595: publication-daemon run, Rule110 dynamic rerun, artifact-suite semantic
4596: validation, unledgered discovery claim, or external venue acceptance, has no
4597: acceptance entry in Table~\ref{tab:current-acceptance-ledger} and also violates
4598: the boundary field in Table~\ref{tab:current-certificate-ledger}.  By
4599: Theorems~\ref{thm:finite-certificate-obstruction-skeleton} and
4600: \ref{thm:evidence-level-overclaim-obstruction}, such a reading is therefore